<main>
  <div class="pagehead">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">Contract · version <span class="num" data-terms-version>–</span></p>
      <h1>RRR Member <em>Agreement</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">The contract you sign when you join. Short and plain on purpose. The full detail sits in the <a href="terms.html">Membership Terms</a>, <a href="code-of-conduct.html">Code of Conduct</a>, <a href="refunds.html">Refund Policy</a> and <a href="privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a>, which are part of this agreement.</p>
      <p class="prov"><span>Draft</span> Beta version. Governed by the laws of England and Wales, without affecting the consumer rights of the country you live in. To be reviewed before launch.</p>
      <div class="ctas-left"><button type="button" class="btn ghost" onclick="window.print()">Print or save as PDF</button><a class="btn primary" href="index.html#join">Join and sign</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="side legal agreement">
    <div class="wrap">
      <article>
        <h2>Between</h2>
        <p><b>Retro Reverb Records</b> ("RRR"), a trading name of Colin David Mathew Bouchard, sole trader, 16 Ashcroft Gardens, Cirencester, Gloucestershire, GL7 1RB, United Kingdom, and <b>you</b>, the person who signs below as an artist member or a fan member.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Everyone agrees</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><b>Membership.</b> You join the RRR Community for a monthly fee (artists <span data-price="artist">€2.00</span>, fans <span data-price="fan">€1.00</span>), paid through PayPal. It renews each month until you cancel.</li>
          <li><b>Cancelling.</b> Cancel any time in PayPal or by email. Your membership runs to the end of the month you've paid for. See the <a href="refunds.html">Refund Policy</a>, including your 14 days to change your mind.</li>
          <li><b>Pausing.</b> Take a break for <span data-price="supporterArtist">€1.00</span> a month (artists) or <span data-price="supporterFan">€0.50</span> (fans). You keep your belt, points and achievements.</li>
          <li><b>Price changes.</b> We tell you at least 30 days before a price change affects you. You can cancel before it does.</li>
          <li><b>Behaviour.</b> You follow the <a href="code-of-conduct.html">Code of Conduct</a>. If you don't, RRR may warn, suspend or remove you as set out there.</li>
          <li><b>Points and cards.</b> Points, belts and digital cards have no cash value and can't be transferred. Points earned unfairly can be removed.</li>
          <li><b>Your data.</b> We use your details only as the <a href="privacy.html">Privacy Policy</a> says. We never sell them.</li>
          <li><b>Leaving.</b> You can leave at any time. RRR can end your membership if you seriously or repeatedly break this agreement.</li>
          <li><b>Your rights.</b> Nothing here takes away your legal rights as a consumer where you live.</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>Artists also agree</h2>
        <ol start="10">
          <li><b>Your music stays yours.</b> You keep all rights in your music, artwork and name, and 100% of your royalties. RRR takes nothing from them; the only deductions are the standard Bandcamp and PayPal charges every Bandcamp artist pays.</li>
          <li><b>Non-exclusive membership.</b> You can release independently and with other labels. Only releases you book with RRR, or submit and RRR approves, become RRR releases, each with the release window and catalogue period below.</li>
          <li><b>Permission to release.</b> For each release you book, you let RRR host it on the RRR Bandcamp catalogue, distribute it to streaming services and promote it, including in discount codes, giveaways and offers. <b>Each release stays in the RRR Bandcamp catalogue permanently</b> through the permanent Bandcamp link. <b>For 18 months RRR is the only distributor sending those exact recordings to streaming services</b>; after that we take them down from streaming within 30 days of asking so you can re-upload them. Bandcamp and YouTube are never exclusive, and remixes, edits and new versions are free to release anywhere. Tracks you agree to put on an RRR compilation stay on it permanently. RRR may also offer it to RRR Bandcamp VIP subscribers early to build interest; VIP subscription money stays with RRR.</li>
          <li><b>Bandcamp link.</b> RRR releases need your Bandcamp linked to the RRR label, by invite or password linking. Fans' payments for your RRR releases go to RRR, and RRR pays them on to your PayPal on the 30th of each month (<a href="terms.html#payouts">Bandcamp payouts</a>). With password linking, RRR only uses access for what the <a href="terms.html#t3">Terms</a> allow and never changes the payment settings of your other releases.</li>
          <li><b>What you promise.</b> You own or have permission for everything you send us, everyone on the release has agreed, you credit collaborators, and you declare AI use honestly (<a href="terms.html#ai">AI policy</a>).</li>
          <li><b>Deadlines.</b> You send your assets on time: at least 2 weeks before release for Bandcamp and 3 weeks for streaming. Late assets can move your release date.</li>
          <li><b>Fees.</b> Upload fees: single <span data-price="single">€2.00</span>, EP <span data-price="ep">€2.50</span>, album <span data-price="album">€3.00</span>, one fee for Bandcamp, streaming or both. YouTube upload <span data-price="youtube">€1.00</span>. Merch listing <span data-price="merch">€2.00</span> per item: merch is sold from your own Bandcamp page and you handle posting and refunds.</li>
        </ol>
      </article>

      <article class="signblock">
        <h2>Signing</h2>
        <p>You sign this agreement on the sign-up form by ticking the box and typing your full legal name. RRR records your name, the date and time, and this version number, and emails you a copy. Your typed name has the same effect as a handwritten signature.</p>
        <div class="sigrow"><span>Member name</span><span>Member ID</span><span>Date</span><span>Version <b class="num" data-terms-version>–</b></span></div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
